<title>BELGIUM: Cementmaker CBR lifts three percent.</title>
<headline>Cementmaker CBR lifts three percent.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Belgium's leading cement maker CBR, a unit of Germany's Heidelberger Zement climbed 3.34 percent on Wednesday as investors flocked to the share after having taken profits in recent weeks.</p>
<p>&quot;The jump comes from the recovery from recent falls, but it could soon reach 3,500 francs,&quot; said one trader.</p>
<p>By 1240 GMT the share stood at 3,400 francs, with 58 million Belgian francs worth of shares traded.</p>
<p>-- Paul de Bendern, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6815, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
